UI and runtime flow changes are easy to break subtly. Prefer conservative edits.

## Interaction + state safety

- Avoid changing **mode transitions**, popup flows, or control lock/enable logic unless required.
- Preserve **keybindings** and dev-mode behavior unless the change explicitly targets them.
- When modifying UI controls, keep layout/measurement logic stable (don’t “clean up” geometry code without a clear need).

## Serialization compatibility

- Be careful with anything that impacts build save/load behavior (XML sections, defaults, migration/conversion prompts).
- Prefer backwards-compatible changes when possible.

